  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Peaceful Uses Initiative</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Support to two projects under IAEA&apos;s Peaceul Uses Initiative targeting developing countries.

A) Sustaining Cradle-to-Grave Control of Radioactive Sources - Phase II:
Objective: To strengthen the safe, secure and sustainable cradle to grave management of sealed radioactive sources (SRS), including disused sealed radioactive sources (DSRS), to protect health and the environment.
Outcome: Enhanced national, regional and interregional infrastructure for the safe, secure and sustainable cradle-to grave management of SRS

B) Strengthening the Capacity to Respond to Radiological Emergencies of Category II and III Facilities (RCA)
Objective: To ensure radiation safety for workers and the public during nuclear or radiological emergencies in the Asia and the Pacific.
Outcome: Capabilities developed among operators and NRAs in the RCA GPs for establishing adequate emergency preparedness and response procedures for category II and III facilities using a graded approach.</narrative>
  </description>
